# AGE domain node values on the ordinary Auto face (PLAN-1095)

The canonical author of the domain node-value family. Every case carries ONE
Auto source; the `av` check runs the ordinary AV language chain
(`ac-av/language-source-run-v1`). Node declarations are admitted on the
ordinary face (CPU-only): the same source is observed by the 979 producer and
the node view text values are asserted through the `nodes` oracle — a real
AV execution, never a static emit claim. No renderer is started; OnEvents /
Scene / NavCall old-parser-only lanes are accounted per the legacy L table,
not this batch.

## Case: node-ordinary-coexist
id: "av.parity.1095.node-ordinary-coexist"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1095", "domain"]
links: ["PLAN-1095"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
fn label() str { return "你好" }
node Hello { view { text label() {} } }
fn main() int { return 42 }
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 42
nodes: { Hello: ["你好"] }

#### stdout

```text
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

§6 contract case: the ordinary chain runs main=42 AND the same source is
observed by the 979 producer (node name/head role + view text values from the
shared execution chain). The `nodes` oracle must observe the text "你好" —
not only the exit code; the renderer is never started.
